# Narrowing the Gap between Concepts and Algorithms in Freshman Chemistry.

**Authors:** Nakhleh, Mary B., And Others

## Abstract
Reports on a study, Project REMODEL, that implemented and evaluated innovations in lecture, laboratory, and assessment for students in the introductory sequence for undergraduate chemistry. Results indicate that special sessions and conceptual exam questions can improve students' abilities to work successfully with both concepts and algorithms. Contains 13 references. (JRH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ530071

